  "notes": "WHAT IS DISTRIBUTED AND WHAT IS NOT. `rust-std` is the precompiled standard library (core, alloc, std and the crates they vendor, including compiler-builtins); it is STATICALLY LINKED into every Domowik binary and is therefore a distributed component with notice obligations. `rustc`, `cargo` and `rust-src` are development-time tools that are never shipped; they are recorded for reproducibility, as docs/THIRD-PARTY-POLICY.md asks.\n\nPROVENANCE OF THE HASHES. Captured 2026-09-12 by a read-only fetch of the official channel manifest https://static.rust-lang.org/dist/channel-rust-1.98.0.toml, authorised by root for that purpose, and transcribed by script rather than by hand. They are `xz_hash` values: they pin THIS RECORD to exact upstream artifacts. NOTHING HERE DOWNLOADS OR VERIFIES AN ARCHIVE AGAINST THEM. Before relying on them for supply-chain verification of a fetched toolchain, add an explicit download-and-hash step.\n\nWHAT IS VERIFIED FAIL-CLOSED on every run: the locally installed rustc version string matches `rustcVersionString`, rust-toolchain.toml's channel matches `channelPin`, and every entry in supportedTargets has a rust-std artifact row.\n\nA STATED GAP. The aggregate copyright notice for the standard library and its vendored components — the upstream COPYRIGHT file, which is where compiler-builtins' `Apache-2.0 WITH LLVM-exception` terms are recorded — is NOT committed to this repository. It ships inside the rust-src archive pinned above. Root's authorisation covered the manifest and its checksums, not downloading and unpacking archives, so this record names the gap instead of asserting a licence text nobody here has read. The wasm32-wasip1 and wasm32-unknown-unknown rust-std rows were added 2026-10-12 for the browser editor (issue 0088) from the same channel manifest's xz_hash values (dist/2026-08-20/channel-rust-1.98.0.toml); the aarch64-apple-darwin row read from that fetch matched the hash recorded above."
